\subsection{What "corrected source data" means}{

\code{rallyr_corrected_rallies()} is the corrected rally table: sentinel speeds
nulled, rallies split at pauses, implausible rallies left out (see
\code{\link[=dq_corrected_rallies]{dq_corrected_rallies()}} for the rules). It is a tibble; a non-R client
should read the schema from \code{\link[=rallyr_api_schema]{rallyr_api_schema()}} and export the tibble to
CSV or Parquet itself. The package does not provide an HTTP layer: build
one (for example with plumber2) only when a real non-R or remote consumer
exists.
}

\subsection{Stability policy (pre-1.0)}{
\itemize{
\item \strong{The contract} is the name and arguments of the functions above and the
name, order and type of each output column (\code{\link[=rallyr_api_schema]{rallyr_api_schema()}}).
Other exported functions are not covered and may change in any release.
\item \strong{Any change to an output shape bumps the minor version} (\verb{0.N.0}) and
\code{\link[=rallyr_schema_version]{rallyr_schema_version()}}, and is listed in \code{NEWS.md}. That includes
adding, removing, renaming, retyping or reordering a column and changing
what a column means. A patch release never changes a shape.
\item \strong{Values change without a shape change} when a data-quality threshold is
recalibrated (\code{\link[=dq_params]{dq_params()}}): more or fewer rows, different values. That is
expected and noted in \code{NEWS.md}. Pass \code{params} explicitly to pin the
thresholds an analysis used.
\item \strong{From 1.0}, ordinary semantic versioning: a breaking shape change is a
major version.
}
}
